BT 1 0 0 1 18 154.8 Tm 12.6 TL /F2 9 Tf .043137 .043137 .043137 rg (Abstract.) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( When developer agents migrate multi-file codebases between sibling libraries such as Python's ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (requests) Tj /F1 9 Tf  T* (\(2.34.2\) and ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (httpx) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(0.28.1\), they encounter the ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Stateful False-Friend Paradox) Tj /F1 9 Tf (: 88.9% \(8/9\) of top-level functions and) Tj T* (83.3% \(10/12\) of core Session/Client methods share identical names, and 12 stateful false-friend API pairs exhibit a) Tj T* (mean 256-dimensional Gemini embedding cosine similarity of ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (0.873) Tj /F1 9 Tf (. Yet their multi-step runtime state machines) Tj T* (diverge silently on redirect following, cross-origin auth stripping, domain-scoped cookie jars, streaming context) Tj T* (lifecycles, and status-exception hierarchies. Across 270 live loopback HTTP state-machine executions \(240 real) Tj T* (Gemma 4 generations + 30 AST codemod runs\), deterministic AST codemods \(Arm 1\) pass 0.0% \(0/30\), while) Tj T* (target-only prompting \(Arm 2\) and fixed HTTP-distractor context \(Arm 3\) both stall at ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (13.3% \(4/30\)) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( on) Tj T* (Gemma-4-31B-IT and ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (13.3% \(4/30\)) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( on Gemma-4-26B-A4B-IT. We introduce ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (StateBridge) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(Arm 4\), which extracts 1) Tj (\226) Tj (2) Tj T* (hop static call-graph state slices from cross-file session initializers. StateBridge raises multi-step wire-equivalence) Tj T* (solve rates to ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (90.0% \(27/30\)) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( on dense Gemma-4-31B-IT \(exact McNemar p = 2.384185791015625e-07\) and ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (96.7%) Tj T* (\(29/30\)) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( on MoE Gemma-4-26B-A4B-IT \(McNemar p = 5.960464477539063e-08\), while an equal-token unrelated) Tj T* (control \(Arm 5\) remains at 16.7% \(5/30\) and 13.3% \(4/30\).) Tj T* ET
